WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.900
When floods come, the water we drink can make us sick.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.510
Floodwater carries sewage into wells, water tanks and food,

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.420
and that spreads several serious diseases.

4
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.100
The same simple steps protect your family from all of them.

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.329
These diseases spread in the same way.

6
00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:21.160
The germs live in the faeces of sick people.

7
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.170
When floodwater or overflowing latrines reach wells, tanks and food,

8
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.439
the germs get in.

9
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.599
Anyone who swallows them can fall ill, and can pass the germs on.

10
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.979
Four of these diseases are worth knowing.

11
00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:39.860
Cholera causes sudden, watery diarrhoea, and can kill within hours.

12
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.670
Dysentery is diarrhoea with blood.

13
00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.070
Typhoid fever brings a high fever that lasts for days,

14
00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.060
with headache and stomach pain.

15
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.330
Hepatitis A and E attack the liver: the eyes and skin turn yellow,

16
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.400
and the urine turns dark.

17
00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.880
Hepatitis E is especially dangerous for pregnant women.

18
00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.199
First, make drinking water safe.

19
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.400
Bring the water to a rolling boil, with big bubbles,

20
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.090
then let it cool with the lid on.

21
00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.800
If you cannot boil it, use water treatment tablets exactly as the packet says.

22
00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:16.680
Use safe water for drinking, cooking, brushing teeth and making baby food.

23
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.979
Second, wash your hands with soap and clean water.

24
00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.310
Wet your hands and rub in soap.

25
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.819
Scrub every part: palms, backs, between the fingers and under the nails.

26
00:01:28.989 --> 00:01:31.500
Rinse, and let them dry in the air.

27
00:01:31.589 --> 00:01:35.470
Do it after the toilet, after cleaning a child, before cooking,

28
00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.820
and before eating or feeding a child.

29
00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.528
Third, keep faeces away from water.

30
00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:46.568
Always use a latrine, never open ground, and keep latrines far from wells.

31
00:01:46.697 --> 00:01:51.128
Put children's faeces in the latrine too, and wash your hands afterwards.

32
00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:54.486
Fourth, make food safe.

33
00:01:54.486 --> 00:01:57.196
Cook food well and eat it while it is hot.

34
00:01:57.326 --> 00:02:01.315
Wash fruit with safe water and peel it, and keep food covered.

35
00:02:02.218 --> 00:02:04.937
If someone gets diarrhoea, act fast.

36
00:02:04.937 --> 00:02:09.178
Start oral rehydration solution, ORS, straight away.

37
00:02:09.178 --> 00:02:14.408
Mix it with safe water exactly as the packet says, and give small sips often.

38
00:02:14.498 --> 00:02:17.648
Keep eating, and keep breastfeeding babies.

39
00:02:17.768 --> 00:02:20.967
Go to a health facility at once if there is blood in the diarrhoea,

40
00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:27.288
a fever that will not go away, or yellow eyes or skin, or if the person is pregnant,

41
00:02:27.288 --> 00:02:29.438
very weak, or cannot drink.

42
00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:33.197
Dysentery and typhoid need medicine from a health worker.

43
00:02:34.078 --> 00:02:37.947
There are vaccines against cholera, typhoid and hepatitis A.

44
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.838
Where health workers offer them, take them,

45
00:02:40.838 --> 00:02:43.627
and keep boiling water and washing hands.

46
00:02:43.878 --> 00:02:47.668
Safe water, clean hands, quick ORS.

47
00:02:47.878 --> 00:02:49.547
Share this with your family.
